"""Self-contained visual replay of the explicitly synthetic tested controller."""
from pathlib import Path
import json

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
fixture=json.loads((ROOT/'tests/project/fixtures/flow-fot-refinement-example.json').read_text())
assert fixture['synthetic'] is True and fixture['training_runs']==0
HTML=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Mora-3 · Flow proposals and forest refinement</title><style>
:root{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#19313f;background:#f4f5f1}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:28px 28px 60px}a{color:#215f60}h1{font-size:clamp(29px,4vw,48px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.035em;max-width:850px;margin:20px 0}h2{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 10px}p{max-width:85ch}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700}.notice{background:#ece9dd;border-left:4px solid #887340;padding:12px 16px;margin:18px 0}.panel{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d4dcda;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin:18px 0}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;align-items:end}label{display:block;font-size:14px;font-weight:650}select,button{min-height:44px;font:inherit;border:1px solid #b6c5c2;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;background:white;color:#19313f;max-width:100%}button{cursor:pointer}button:hover,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #52877f;outline-offset:2px}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin:20px 0}.metric{border-top:2px solid #64847c;padding-top:10px}.metric strong{display:block;font-size:30px}.small{font-size:13px;color:#52636b}.scroll{overflow:auto;max-width:100%}.scroll>svg{display:block;min-width:740px;width:100%;height:auto}#forest>svg{min-width:0}.selected-output{display:inline-block;background:#e4f0ea;border:1px solid #6d9483;padding:8px 12px;margin:5px;border-radius:6px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr;gap:20px}.grid>div{min-width:0}.label-note{font-size:13px;font-weight:600}.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#candidate-summary{min-height:90px}svg [role=button]{cursor:pointer}svg [role=button]:focus{outline:3px solid #316c66}footer{border-top:1px solid #d4dcda;padding-top:18px;margin-top:24px} @media(max-width:700px){main{padding:20px 14px 40px}.panel{padding:15px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.metrics{gap:10px}.metric strong{font-size:24px}.controls>*{width:100%}select,button{width:100%}} @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto}}
</style></head><body><main><a href="../index.html">Mora-3 research</a><p class="eyebrow">Inference controller · complete forests · multiple outputs</p><h1>Propose several. Refine the forest.<br>Keep more than one result.</h1><p>Independent flow proposals seed a candidate pool. Whole-forest checks guide bounded subtree corrections. Original candidates remain available, and final decoding is checked again before several distinct outputs are returned.</p><div class="notice"><strong>Synthetic controller replay, not trained model performance.</strong> These values come from the implemented Python controller with an analytic two-dimensional field and an illustrative score. No biomedical data, trained checkpoint, optimizer update or verified reasoning gain is represented.</div><div class="controls"><label>Completed edit rounds<select id="rounds"><option value="0">0 · initial proposals only</option><option value="1">1 · first corrections</option><option value="2" selected>2 · further refinement</option></select></label><label>Inspect full candidate forest<select id="candidate"></select></label><button id="export-svg">Export lineage SVG</button><button id="export-json">Export this replay</button></div><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><span>Initial proposals</span><strong id="initial-count"></strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Proposals including edits</span><strong id="candidate-count"></strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Distinct checked outputs</span><strong id="output-count"></strong></div></div><section class="panel"><h2>Every revision keeps its parent</h2><p class="small">Arrows link an edited candidate to its unmodified predecessor. Green outlines mark returned outputs. Click or keyboard-select any candidate to inspect all its branches below.</p><p class="small">On narrow screens, scroll the lineage diagram horizontally; the complete candidate forest below fits the screen.</p><div class="scroll" id="lineage" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable candidate lineage"></div><div id="outputs" aria-live="polite"></div></section><section class="panel grid"><div><h2>Complete selected forest</h2><div class="scroll" id="forest"></div></div><div><h2>Candidate evidence</h2><div id="candidate-summary" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="small">The fixed condition is never edited. A subtree correction replaces that node and all its descendants; the sibling branch is preserved. Replacements receive new identities and fresh verification.</p></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>What is being measured?</h2><p>The fixture score is the mean of <span class="mono">exp(−z₁²)</span> over every non-condition node. It rewards a simple analytic property, not truth or biological feasibility. The second coordinate retains alternative values. Tokenization in this fixture is numerical quantization, not Mora-3's unfinished trained token-forest decoder.</p><p id="compute" class="small"></p><p>Production use requires source-bound model, score and decoder implementations. Unknown or failed checks do not become successful outputs. A request for three outputs may return fewer when quality or diversity requirements cannot be met. Selection and edits change the distribution: these results are not unmodified on-policy GFlowNet samples.</p></section><footer class="small"><p>Method source: <a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/bi25a.html">Bi et al., Forest-of-Thought, ICML 2025</a>, sections 3.1–3.3. The paper provides sparse activation, dynamic self-correction and consensus/expert decision-making. Flow-generated latent forests, explicit subtree replacement and a multi-output result API are Mora-3 adaptations.</p><p>Related: <a href="flow-forest.html">flow-forest architecture</a> · <a href="persistence-vectors.html">persistence laboratory</a> · <a href="../paper.html#flow-fot-refinement">live paper</a></p></footer></main><script id="fixture-data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
'use strict';const DATA=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('fixture-data').textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id),NS='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
let round=2,candidate=null;const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
function source(){return DATA.snapshots[round]}
function shell(body,w,h,title){return `<svg xmlns="${NS}" viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" role="img" aria-label="${esc(title)}"><title>${esc(title)}</title><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10" fill="#8a9c9b"/></marker></defs><rect width="${w}" height="${h}" fill="#ffffff"/>${body}</svg>`}
function lineage(){const s=source(),rows=s.candidates,pos=new Map(),width=1050,step=315;let body='',max=0;
for(let r=0;r<=round;r++){const group=rows.filter(x=>x.round===r);max=Math.max(max,group.length);body+=`<text x="${150+r*step}" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-family="system-ui" fill="#19313f">${r===0?'Flow proposals':'Edit round '+r}</text>`;group.forEach((x,j)=>pos.set(x.candidate_id,{x:150+r*step,y:65+j*63}));}
for(const x of rows){if(x.parent_id===null)continue;const a=pos.get(x.parent_id),b=pos.get(x.candidate_id);body+=`<path d="M${a.x+98} ${a.y+20}C${a.x+155} ${a.y+20},${b.x-155} ${b.y+20},${b.x-100} ${b.y+20}" fill="none" stroke="#aab8b4" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>`;}
for(const x of rows){const p=pos.get(x.candidate_id),output=s.output_ids.includes(x.candidate_id),selected=x.candidate_id===candidate;body+=`<g role="button" tabindex="0" data-id="${x.candidate_id}" aria-label="Inspect candidate ${x.candidate_id}, score ${x.score.toFixed(5)}"><title>Candidate ${x.candidate_id} · ${esc(x.operation)} · score ${x.score}</title><rect x="${p.x-98}" y="${p.y}" width="196" height="43" rx="7" fill="${output?'#e4f0ea':'#f7f8f5'}" stroke="${selected?'#19313f':output?'#477c65':'#c8d1ce'}" stroke-width="${selected?3:output?2:1}"/><text x="${p.x-84}" y="${p.y+18}" font-family="system-ui" font-weight="650" font-size="13" fill="#19313f">C${x.candidate_id}${output?' · returned':''}</text><text x="${p.x+84}" y="${p.y+18}" text-anchor="end" font-family="monospace" font-size="12" fill="#19313f">${x.score.toFixed(5)}</text><text x="${p.x-84}" y="${p.y+33}" font-family="system-ui" font-size="10" fill="#52636b">${esc(x.operation.replaceAll('_',' '))}</text></g>`}
return shell(body,width,Math.max(220,90+max*63),'Synthetic flow proposal and correction lineage')}
function forest(row){const width=Math.min(740,Math.max(320,window.innerWidth-60));const n=row.parents.length,children=Array.from({length:n},()=>[]),depth=Array(n).fill(0),xs=Array(n).fill(0);row.parents.forEach((p,i)=>{if(p>=0){children[p].push(i);depth[i]=depth[p]+1}});const leaves=children.map((c,i)=>c.length?null:i).filter(i=>i!==null);leaves.forEach((i,j)=>xs[i]=(j+1)*width/(leaves.length+1));for(let i=n-1;i>=0;i--)if(children[i].length)xs[i]=children[i].reduce((v,j)=>v+xs[j],0)/children[i].length;let b='';const half=Math.min(90,width/(leaves.length+1)/2-6);const y=i=>30+depth[i]*100;
row.parents.forEach((p,i)=>{if(p>=0)b+=`<path d="M${xs[p]} ${y(p)+52}L${xs[i]} ${y(i)-5}" stroke="#8a9c9b" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>`});for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const fixed=row.clamped.includes(i);b+=`<rect x="${xs[i]-half}" y="${y(i)}" width="${2*half}" height="55" rx="6" fill="${fixed?'#e7e9ef':'#f0f6f1'}" stroke="#9caaa6"/><text x="${xs[i]}" y="${y(i)+16}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui" font-size="12" fill="#19313f">${fixed?(width<500?'Fixed':'Fixed condition'):row.statuses[i]+' · '+i}</text><text x="${xs[i]}" y="${y(i)+34}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#19313f">[${row.states[i].map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(', ')}]</text><text x="${xs[i]}" y="${y(i)+48}" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui" font-size="10" fill="#52636b">node score ${row.node_scores[i].toFixed(3)}</text>`}return shell(b,width,110+Math.max(...depth)*100,'Complete candidate forest with both branches and fixed root')}
function render(){const s=source();if(!s.candidates.some(x=>x.candidate_id===candidate))candidate=s.output_ids[0]??0;$('rounds').value=String(round);$('candidate').innerHTML=s.candidates.map(x=>`<option value="${x.candidate_id}">C${x.candidate_id} · score ${x.score.toFixed(5)}</option>`).join('');$('candidate').value=String(candidate);$('initial-count').textContent=s.candidates.filter(x=>x.parent_id===null).length;$('candidate-count').textContent=s.candidate_attempts;$('output-count').textContent=s.output_ids.length;$('lineage').innerHTML=lineage();const row=s.candidates.find(x=>x.candidate_id===candidate);$('forest').innerHTML=forest(row);$('candidate-summary').innerHTML=`<p><strong>Candidate C${candidate}</strong><br>${esc(row.operation.replaceAll('_',' '))}<br>Parent: ${row.parent_id===null?'initial proposal':'C'+row.parent_id}<br>Whole-forest score: <strong>${row.score.toFixed(8)}</strong><br>Verifier status: ${esc(row.status)}</p><p class="small mono">Content binding: ${row.fingerprint.slice(0,20)}…</p>`;$('outputs').innerHTML=s.output_ids.map((id,i)=>`<span class="selected-output">C${id} · decoded score ${s.output_scores[i].toFixed(5)}</span>`).join('');$('compute').textContent=`${s.velocity_evaluations} batched velocity calls generated six initial forests. ${s.counts.edit_callback_calls} edit callbacks, ${s.counts.full_forest_assessments} whole-forest assessments and ${s.counts.decoder_calls} decoding checks were executed. Callback-internal compute must be measured separately in production.`;$('lineage').querySelectorAll('[data-id]').forEach(el=>{const choose=()=>{candidate=Number(el.dataset.id);render()};el.onclick=choose;el.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();choose()}}});history.replaceState(null,'',`#r=${round}&c=${candidate}`);window.RefinementExplorer.ready=true}
function download(text,name,type){const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text],{type}));a.download=name;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),500)}
window.addEventListener('resize',()=>{const r=source().candidates.find(x=>x.candidate_id===candidate);if(r)$('forest').innerHTML=forest(r)});window.RefinementExplorer={ready:false,source,svg:()=>lineage(),snapshot:()=>({round,candidate,outputs:source().output_ids,source_code:DATA.source_code_sha256})};$('rounds').onchange=()=>{round=Number($('rounds').value);candidate=null;render()};$('candidate').onchange=()=>{candidate=Number($('candidate').value);render()};$('export-svg').onclick=()=>download(lineage(),'flow-fot-refinement.svg','image/svg+xml');$('export-json').onclick=()=>download(JSON.stringify({synthetic:true,training_runs:0,selected:source()},null,2),'flow-fot-refinement.json','application/json');const hash=new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1));if(['0','1','2'].includes(hash.get('r')))round=Number(hash.get('r'));if(/^\d+$/.test(hash.get('c')||''))candidate=Number(hash.get('c'));render();
</script></body></html>'''
page=HTML.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(fixture,separators=(',',':')).replace('<','\\u003c'))
path=ROOT/'docs/project/flow-fot-refinement.html';path.write_text(page)
print(json.dumps(dict(page=str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),bytes=path.stat().st_size,synthetic=True)))
